From c9edb433e064803fef92d488c7e66d078c06cde0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:38:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: draw GS viewport selections as ordered runs
 biblioklept

GS viewport-index selection was emulated with FS clipping and a GPU
geometric clipper. Replace it with GPU-built ordered viewport runs
(libpan vp_runs.cl): each run of consecutive primitives sharing a
viewport is drawn as its own IDVS draw, with that viewport's hardware
LOW/HIGH_DEPTH_CLAMP computed by the shared native helper
(panvk_viewport_depth_range). The run list is built after each GS chunk,
before TESS_READY, so tess-fed GS draws replay it per chunk. Overflow
discards the draw rather than keeping a prefix. v12 keeps the old path
since its depth clamp lives in the viewport register. Adds a host test
for the run builder.

Generated-by: LLM
